Data credits
------------
This project ships no data. All data used in its published results is simulated.

- Sparkov Data Generation, by Brandon Harris. Sparkov is the simulator that produced the card
  transactions. A copy is published on Kaggle as kartik2112/fraud-detection under the CC0
  public-domain licence.
- Fraud Dataset Benchmark (FDB), by Amazon Science
  (https://github.com/amazon-science/fraud-dataset-benchmark). Its "sparknov" dataset is this Sparkov
  copy. This project uses it so results can be compared with published baselines.

How to get the data
-------------------
You download it yourself. Run `fraud load`, with a Kaggle token in KAGGLE_API_TOKEN,
~/.kaggle/access_token or ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json. The command downloads the two source files from
Kaggle, checks them against pinned sha256 hashes, drops personal and location columns and writes the
splits to the git-ignored `data/` folder. No data file is committed to this repository, and a test
checks that. DATA_CARD.md describes the data in full.

